      "facts": [
        "(USER_MEMORY_TOKENS) before older tool history competes for the rest.",
        "What a mechanical pass may add, beyond MECHANICAL_HISTORY_TOKENS and only out of room the window really has, to keep the user's earlier requests and the newest to-do list.",
        "Below this, a shortened earlier request says too little to be worth keeping.",
        "The user's earlier requests and the newest to-do list first, out of their own allowance (USER_MEMORY_TOKENS), newest first; a request too large for what is left is shortened rather than skipped.",
        "Only out of room under the pass's own target as well as the window, so a pass still lands well below its trigger and does not compact again at once.",
        "Older tool history goes first; the reserved requests only if that is not enough."
